];

const faq = [
  { q: 'Are ravens the smartest birds?', a: 'Ravens are among the cognitively most advanced birds, but "smartest bird" is a problematic claim. New Caledonian Crows excel at tool use; African Grey Parrots show strong referential communication; ravens lead on certain planning and social cognition tasks. No single species is best at all cognitive tasks, and intelligence is not a single dimension.' },
  { q: 'Are ravens smarter than parrots?', a: 'Ravens and parrots (particularly African Greys and keas) are cognitively comparable but differently specialised. Ravens excel at social cognition, planning, and cache protection. African Greys show stronger referential communication. Keas show flexible problem-solving. Neither is simply "smarter."' },
  { q: 'Are ravens smarter than dogs?', a: 'Ravens outperform dogs on most tasks involving physical causality, planning for the future, and certain social cognition tasks. Dogs outperform ravens on tasks involving reading human communicative cues (pointing, gaze direction). The comparison depends entirely on the task.' },
];
---

